1
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,180
My daughter was asleep at home when the

2
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:12,880
school intercom called her name.

3
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:16,140
I know she was asleep because my wife

4
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:18,460
had sent me a picture ten minutes earlier.

5
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:21,680
Ellie was curled around a stuffed rabbit,

6
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:24,740
one sock on, one sock somewhere under the

7
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:25,240
blankets.

8
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:29,060
Then at exactly three in the morning,

9
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:31,860
a woman's voice came
through the speaker above

10
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:32,580
my desk.

11
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:34,780
Eleanor Brooks.

12
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,400
Nobody calls my daughter Eleanor,

13
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:40,080
not even her mother.

14
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:43,540
I reached for the radio, thinking someone had

15
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:44,500
gotten into the building.

16
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:46,560
Before I could press the button,

17
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:48,360
a second voice came through.

18
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:49,800
Small,

19
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:51,040
sleepy,

20
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:53,140
unmistakably hers.

21
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:57,780
Here. My phone started vibrating.

22
00:00:58,120 --> 00:00:59,440
It was my wife.

23
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,640
Dan, she said,

24
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:04,240
why is Ellie's bedroom door locked?

25
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:08,000
I'd been working nights
at Bellwether Elementary for

26
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:08,940
11 days.

27
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:11,200
It wasn't interesting work.

28
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:14,840
Check the exterior doors, walk the corridors,

29
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:18,380
write down anything leaking,
broken, or expensive enough

30
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:19,520
that someone might care.

31
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:23,180
My daughter attended the school, which was how

32
00:01:23,180 --> 00:01:24,380
I'd heard about the job.

33
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:27,280
She liked knowing I was there after everyone

34
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:28,040
went home.

35
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:31,000
Said I was keeping her classroom safe.

36
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:33,760
The building had three wings.

37
00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:35,580
Two were still in use.

38
00:01:36,260 --> 00:01:38,160
The third had been closed since a fire

39
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:39,180
in 1987.

40
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:42,700
The head custodian, Frank,
showed me the chained

41
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:44,060
doors on my first shift.

42
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:47,140
No patrols past this point, he said.

43
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:48,860
Structural damage?

44
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:51,280
That's what the paperwork says.

45
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:53,820
Then he handed me a key ring.

46
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,200
One key had a strip of red tape

47
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:59,200
around it. That opens the west stairwell.

48
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:01,320
Fire department requires access.

49
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:03,580
He held on to it for a second

50
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:04,560
before letting go.

51
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:07,540
If you hear anybody over there,

52
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:08,660
call me.

53
00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:11,060
I asked if kids ever broke in.

54
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:13,520
Frank looked through the wired glass.

55
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:15,500
Just call me.

56
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:18,300
The first time the intercom came on,

57
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:19,720
I thought it was a fault.

58
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:21,600
Three short tones.

59
00:02:22,460 --> 00:02:23,660
A woman clearing her throat.

60
00:02:23,660 --> 00:02:25,660
Michael Turner.

61
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:27,040
A pause.

62
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:28,740
Rebecca Shaw.

63
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:30,340
Another pause.

64
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:32,720
She read 18 names.

65
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,100
Then she said,

66
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:36,080
We're still waiting for one.

67
00:02:37,380 --> 00:02:38,700
The speaker clicked off.

68
00:02:40,490 --> 00:02:41,980
I checked every classroom.

69
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:43,900
Nothing.

70
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:45,860
The next afternoon,

71
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:48,440
Frank told me the old public address system

72
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:50,400
sometimes picked up radio interference.

73
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:54,060
I asked what station broadcast
school attendance at

74
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:54,940
three in the morning.

75
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:56,820
He didn't answer.

76
00:02:57,700 --> 00:03:00,300
The following night, I recorded it.

77
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:01,520
Same woman,

78
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:03,280
same 18 names,

79
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:04,940
same pauses.

80
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:06,600
But this time,

81
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:08,840
just before the speaker went dead,

82
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:11,660
I heard a chair scrape across the floor.

83
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:13,700
Then a child whispered,

84
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:16,180
she knows about the new girl.

85
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:18,220
I played that part for Frank.

86
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:19,920
He listened without moving.

87
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:22,340
Then he asked whether Ellie had ever been

88
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:23,360
near the West Wing.

89
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:25,920
I told him no, that was what I

90
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:26,480
believed,

91
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:29,440
until I remembered the drawing
she'd brought home.

92
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:32,640
A week earlier, Ellie had drawn a classroom,

93
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:34,400
19 desks,

94
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:35,980
18 children.

95
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:38,700
A woman colored entirely in gray.

96
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:41,240
At the back was a red door with

97
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:42,040
no handle.

98
00:03:42,820 --> 00:03:44,300
I'd asked if that was her teacher.

99
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:47,380
No, that's the lady who found me.

100
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:50,080
Ellie had gotten separated from her class during

101
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:51,140
a library visit.

102
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:53,260
She said the gray lady had shown her

103
00:03:53,260 --> 00:03:54,040
the way back.

104
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:56,060
I assumed she meant a substitute.

105
00:03:56,660 --> 00:03:58,580
Now my wife was on the phone outside

106
00:03:58,580 --> 00:03:59,880
our daughter's locked bedroom.

107
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:01,560
Can you hear her?

108
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:02,280
I asked.

109
00:04:02,940 --> 00:04:03,580
Talking.

110
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:04,720
To who?

111
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:05,920
I don't know.

112
00:04:06,460 --> 00:04:07,600
I heard my wife knock.

113
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:10,060
Then Ellie spoke from the other side.

114
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:13,040
Mommy, you have to wait until attendance is

115
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:13,540
finished.

116
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:15,820
Above me the intercom crackled.

117
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:17,200
The woman said,

118
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:19,620
Eleanor, please keep your eyes on the front.

119
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:21,980
My wife began hitting the bedroom door.

120
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:23,940
I told her to get the spare key.

121
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:25,780
She said she already had.

122
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:27,520
It turned in the lock.

123
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,200
The door wouldn't move.

124
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:30,680
I called Frank.

125
00:04:31,140 --> 00:04:32,420
He answered on the first ring.

126
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:33,900
She said, here.

127
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:34,820
I told him.

128
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:36,880
For a moment, I could hear nothing but

129
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:37,440
his breathing.

130
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:38,700
Frank?

131
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:40,360
don't leave the building.

132
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:41,360
What?

133
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:44,140
If you leave, you won't find the room

134
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:46,520
again tonight. I started running toward the west

135
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:46,900
wing.

136
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:48,960
Tell me what this is.

137
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:51,000
Is there a chair outside the classroom?

138
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:53,500
I'm not in the classroom.

139
00:04:54,140 --> 00:04:55,480
You will be.

140
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:56,880
Listen carefully.

141
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:59,200
There'll be a chair in the hall.

142
00:04:59,780 --> 00:05:01,860
Under it, there's a folder.

143
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:04,300
My wife called again.

144
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:05,560
I switched lines.

145
00:05:06,380 --> 00:05:08,580
She was crying so hard I could barely

146
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:09,520
understand her.

147
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:12,120
The bedroom door had opened.

148
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:13,920
Ellie wasn't inside.

149
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:16,120
The window was locked.

150
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:18,040
Her rabbit was still in bed.

151
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:20,540
And there was something on the pillow.

152
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:23,760
A little rectangle of yellow paper.

153
00:05:24,940 --> 00:05:26,560
My wife read it to me.

154
00:05:27,180 --> 00:05:28,580
Eleanor Brooks,

155
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:30,280
room 19.

156
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:32,920
At the end of the corridor,

157
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:35,240
beyond the chained doors, a light came on.

158
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:38,520
Then I heard my daughter scream.

159
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:40,620
Daddy?

160
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:43,520
I used the red key.

161
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:46,700
The air changed as soon as I crossed

162
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:47,560
the stairwell,

163
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:49,380
warm,

164
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:50,680
chalky.

165
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:54,580
It smelled like wet wool drying on a

166
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:55,140
radiator.

167
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:58,720
The corridor should have ended at a collapsed

168
00:05:58,720 --> 00:05:59,680
section of roof.

169
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:04,220
Instead, it continued past rows of coat hooks.

170
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:07,680
At the far end stood a red door,

171
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:11,860
room 19. There was a small wooden chair

172
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:13,000
beside it.

173
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:14,560
Under the chair,

174
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:15,820
a folder.

175
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:17,520
On the cover,

176
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:19,960
Emergency Student Release.

177
00:06:21,020 --> 00:06:23,200
Inside were carbon copy forms.

178
00:06:23,960 --> 00:06:24,800
Most were blank.

179
00:06:25,740 --> 00:06:28,420
One had been completed in faded blue ink.

180
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:29,920
Student,

181
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:31,880
Thomas Mercer.

182
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:33,520
Release to,

183
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:34,920
Ann Mercer.

184
00:06:35,620 --> 00:06:37,200
Below that was another line.

185
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:39,800
Adult remaining on premises.

186
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:41,500
Ann Mercer.

187
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:43,220
I turned the page.

188
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,180
A newspaper clipping had been folded behind the

189
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:46,620
form.

190
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:49,880
Local mother missing after school search.

191
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:52,120
October 1994.

192
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:55,260
In the photograph, a little boy stood beside

193
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:56,220
a police officer.

194
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:58,440
Someone had circled his face.

195
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:02,100
Below it, in handwriting I recognized from the

196
00:07:02,100 --> 00:07:04,680
maintenance log, He came home.

197
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:06,200
I called Frank.

198
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:08,080
Who's Thomas Mercer?

199
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:10,240
My name, he said.

200
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:12,040
My middle name is Frank.

201
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:13,800
Frank had been seven.

202
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:16,200
He'd followed a woman into the West Wing

203
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,420
during a school assembly.

204
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:20,060
His mother came looking for him that night.

205
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:21,860
Only he came back.

206
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:24,460
I remember her coat, he said.

207
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:26,820
She put it around me before she opened

208
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:27,320
the door.

209
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:29,180
You knew this could happen?

210
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:31,000
I knew what happened to me.

211
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:32,660
Why didn't you tell me?

212
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,300
I heard the recording.

213
00:07:35,020 --> 00:07:36,080
I should have told you then.

214
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:38,040
I wanted to scream at him.

215
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:41,140
Instead, I asked how to get Ellie out.

216
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:42,420
The form,

217
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:43,320
he said.

218
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:44,900
Fill in the release.

219
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:46,700
Slide it under the door.

220
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:48,240
Then the last line?

221
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:49,600
He didn't answer.

222
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:52,520
Through the wall, I heard pencils moving across

223
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:53,040
paper.

224
00:07:53,620 --> 00:07:54,240
Frank,

225
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,080
what happens to the adult?

226
00:07:56,520 --> 00:07:57,440
I don't know.

227
00:07:57,860 --> 00:07:58,480
Your mother?

228
00:07:59,040 --> 00:08:00,240
Sometimes I hear her.

229
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,900
His voice broke,

230
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:03,300
through the vents,

231
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:04,840
mostly in winter.

232
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:06,460
Inside the classroom,

233
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:09,200
a woman tapped something against the desk.

234
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:10,420
Eleanor,

235
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:12,660
your father is making us wait.

236
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:14,460
My daughter began to cry.

237
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,220
I took out my pen.

238
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:17,940
I wrote Ellie's name,

239
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,760
my name beneath it,

240
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:20,680
father.

241
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:23,000
Then I stopped at the final line,

242
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:25,320
adult remaining on-premises.

243
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:27,540
There was a space for a signature.

244
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:30,140
I thought about calling the police,

245
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:33,820
explaining that my daughter had vanished from a

246
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:37,120
locked bedroom and was now inside a

247
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:38,900
classroom that shouldn't exist.

248
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:43,280
I thought about breaking the door down.

249
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:46,160
Then I looked through the little square of

250
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:46,800
glass.

251
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:49,340
Ellie sat at the front,

252
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:52,760
bare feet, Yellow pajamas.

253
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:56,420
Behind her were 18 children.

254
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:59,140
Some wore clothes like the ones in my

255
00:08:59,140 --> 00:09:00,320
own school photographs.

256
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:02,640
Others looked much older.

257
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:05,520
All of them were watching the door.

258
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:07,740
Ellie saw me.

259
00:09:08,220 --> 00:09:09,540
She started to stand.

260
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:13,060
A gray hand settled on her shoulder.

261
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:15,960
Seated until you're dismissed.

262
00:09:16,980 --> 00:09:18,200
I signed.

263
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:20,400
Slid the paper underneath.

264
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:23,000
The pencil sound stopped,

265
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:25,700
something moved on the other side.

266
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:28,080
Then the form came back,

267
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:31,360
a neat red check beside my signature.

268
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:33,620
The handle turned,

269
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:36,160
Ellie ran into my arms,

270
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:37,820
she was warm,

271
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:39,120
real.

272
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:42,340
I could feel her heart hammering against my

273
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:42,820
chest.

274
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,740
Daddy, she wouldn't let me wake up.

275
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:48,280
I kissed the top of her head.

276
00:09:48,980 --> 00:09:49,880
Behind her,

277
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:52,040
the woman stood at the blackboard,

278
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:54,020
a gray cardigan,

279
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:55,640
a long skirt.

280
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:59,260
Her face looked almost ordinary until I tried

281
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:00,460
to focus on it.

282
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:02,260
Then it seemed to shift,

283
00:10:03,020 --> 00:10:04,900
like a face remembered from a dream.

284
00:10:05,780 --> 00:10:07,660
Your daughter has been released, Mr.

285
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:07,940
Brooks.

286
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:10,900
I stood with Ellie in my arms,

287
00:10:11,940 --> 00:10:13,380
took one step backward.

288
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:15,880
My daughter crossed the threshold.

289
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:17,960
I didn't.

290
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:19,620
There was no wall,

291
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:21,740
nothing pressing against me.

292
00:10:22,420 --> 00:10:24,620
My legs simply stopped obeying.

293
00:10:25,340 --> 00:10:27,500
I lowered Ellie onto the corridor floor,

294
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:29,120
keeping hold of her hand.

295
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:31,520
Then I tried again.

296
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:34,940
Pain shot from my wrist to my shoulder.

297
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:37,180
The woman watched.

298
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:41,160
Children must be collected
by an authorized adult.

299
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:43,640
I looked at the form in her hand.

300
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:46,040
And an adult must remain,

301
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:47,940
she smiled,

302
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:50,020
You've read it correctly.

303
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:52,860
I could have pulled Ellie back inside,

304
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:55,460
that's the part I need you to understand.

305
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:59,320
For one terrible second, I almost did,

306
00:11:00,040 --> 00:11:01,600
because she was holding my hand.

307
00:11:02,340 --> 00:11:03,580
Because I was afraid,

308
00:11:04,380 --> 00:11:06,020
because I wanted more time.

309
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:07,820
Then I heard Frank,

310
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:10,000
still on the phone in my pocket.

311
00:11:11,780 --> 00:11:13,600
Daniel. I put him on speaker.

312
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:16,000
Get to the west stairwell.

313
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:17,420
I'm coming.

314
00:11:18,220 --> 00:11:19,200
I looked at Ellie.

315
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:21,100
Remember the fire drill?

316
00:11:21,700 --> 00:11:22,420
She nodded.

317
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:24,500
Walk to the stairs.

318
00:11:25,180 --> 00:11:25,980
Hold the rail.

319
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:27,740
Frank will be there.

320
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:29,340
Come with me.

321
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:31,340
I have to finish something.

322
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:32,980
You're lying.

323
00:11:33,780 --> 00:11:35,720
I'd never heard her say that before.

324
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:38,000
I took off my wedding ring,

325
00:11:38,780 --> 00:11:39,860
pressed it into her palm.

326
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:41,780
Give this to mom.

327
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:43,600
She shook her head.

328
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:46,460
Behind me, chairs scraped backward.

329
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:48,600
The teacher said my name.

330
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:50,800
This time it sounded like a warning.

331
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:52,980
I let go of Ellie's hand.

332
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:54,260
Go.

333
00:11:55,020 --> 00:11:56,380
She took two steps,

334
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:57,860
then turned.

335
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:00,120
I made myself smile.

336
00:12:01,040 --> 00:12:02,220
It must have looked terrible.

337
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:05,760
But she took another step, then another.

338
00:12:06,580 --> 00:12:08,640
I watched until she reached the stairs,

339
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:10,960
until Frank picked her up,

340
00:12:11,660 --> 00:12:13,500
until I couldn't hear her calling anymore.

341
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:16,140
There was an empty desk at the back,

342
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:18,020
too small for me.

343
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:19,660
I sat anyway.

344
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:22,460
The woman walked between the rows,

345
00:12:23,220 --> 00:12:24,720
checking each child's work.

346
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:26,860
Nobody looked up.

347
00:12:27,300 --> 00:12:28,620
I took out my phone.

348
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:30,260
No signal.

349
00:12:31,220 --> 00:12:32,580
The call with Frank had ended.

350
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:35,460
The time still read three o 'clock.

351
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:37,760
Then someone touched my sleeve.

352
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:40,280
A woman sat beside me.

353
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:41,540
Brown coat.

354
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:44,120
Dark hair pinned behind one ear.

355
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:46,800
I hadn't seen her when I came in.

356
00:12:47,380 --> 00:12:48,160
Did he get out?

357
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:49,340
She whispered.

358
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:51,140
I knew who she meant.

359
00:12:52,020 --> 00:12:52,460
Yes.

360
00:12:53,180 --> 00:12:54,480
She closed her eyes.

361
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:57,200
For a moment, she looked younger.

362
00:12:58,180 --> 00:12:59,160
Did he have a good life?

363
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:00,700
I think he...

364
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:02,680
I thought of Frank's lunch in the staff

365
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:03,480
refrigerator.

366
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:07,140
The photographs of his
grandchildren taped inside his

367
00:13:07,140 --> 00:13:07,600
locker.

368
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:10,100
Yes, I said.

369
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:11,760
I think he did.

370
00:13:12,540 --> 00:13:13,300
She nodded.

371
00:13:14,340 --> 00:13:15,820
Then she looked toward the front.

372
00:13:16,780 --> 00:13:17,980
She'll ask you to help.

373
00:13:18,820 --> 00:13:22,360
With what? The teacher placed a register on

374
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:23,060
my desk.

375
00:13:24,020 --> 00:13:25,160
19 names.

376
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,300
18 I recognized from the recording.

377
00:13:29,340 --> 00:13:30,760
The last was mine.

378
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:33,780
There are other children waiting, she said.

379
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:36,740
We need someone with a familiar voice.

380
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:38,760
I pushed the book away.

381
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:40,420
She placed it back.

382
00:13:41,140 --> 00:13:42,320
You work here now.

383
00:13:43,100 --> 00:13:45,020
Beside me, Ann Mercer whispered,

384
00:13:45,980 --> 00:13:47,280
don't read the names.

385
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:49,700
I don't know how long I've been here.

386
00:13:50,540 --> 00:13:52,140
My phone battery hasn't moved.

387
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:53,900
Neither has the clock.

388
00:13:54,820 --> 00:13:56,620
Sometimes the room goes dark and I can

389
00:13:56,620 --> 00:13:58,060
hear the school outside,

390
00:13:58,780 --> 00:13:59,880
floor polishers,

391
00:14:01,260 --> 00:14:02,760
basketballs. Once,

392
00:14:03,540 --> 00:14:04,420
children singing.

393
00:14:04,980 --> 00:14:06,040
I tried shouting.

394
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:07,520
Nobody heard.

395
00:14:08,220 --> 00:14:08,980
But yesterday,

396
00:14:09,540 --> 00:14:11,520
the speaker above the blackboard clicked.

397
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:14,260
And for a second I heard Frank.

398
00:14:14,980 --> 00:14:17,900
He was testing the intercom,
which means something

399
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:19,240
can still pass through.

400
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:21,060
So I'm recording this.

401
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:22,820
If you hear it,

402
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:24,140
find my wife.

403
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:26,660
Tell her Ellie got out before the door

404
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:27,200
closed.

405
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,840
Tell her I saw Frank take her.

406
00:14:30,460 --> 00:14:31,260
And tell Ellie.

407
00:14:31,980 --> 00:14:33,560
Tell Ellie I'm sorry I couldn't walk her

408
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:34,280
to the stairs.

409
00:14:34,940 --> 00:14:35,860
The teacher's coming.

410
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:37,920
She's carrying the register.

411
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:40,380
There's a new name on the last page.

412
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,040
I'm covering it.

413
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:43,600
I won't read it.

414
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:46,120
If this recording reaches another school,

415
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:47,380
turn off your speakers.

416
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:49,100
Wake your children.

417
00:14:49,760 --> 00:14:51,460
And if a voice calls their name,

418
00:14:52,180 --> 00:14:53,580
make sure they don't answer.

419
00:14:54,660 --> 00:14:56,740
Wait, she's standing beside me.

420
00:14:57,220 --> 00:14:58,440
She's looking at the register.

421
00:14:58,860 --> 00:15:00,260
That isn't a new name.

422
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:02,440
She's calling my daughter again.

423
00:15:03,140 --> 00:15:03,900
Eleanor Brooks,

424
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:05,500
thank you for listening.

425
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:07,580
If you'd like to hear more stories like

426
00:15:07,580 --> 00:15:09,060
this, subscribe to the channel.

427
00:15:10,060 --> 00:15:10,920
Until the next story,

428
00:15:11,780 --> 00:15:12,220
sleep well.
